{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545346-appearance-and-paths","id":1545346,"title":"Appearance and Paths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-04T15:53:19-08:00","id":1545346,"title":"Appearance and Paths","content":"Starting a V20 game. One of the Elder NPCs is on the Path of Honorable Accord. The ability to pass for human varies with Humanity. For one on a path, is a corpse-like visage the default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T16:26:40-08:00","id":1545350,"title":"","content":"V20 Core is a bit mixed on this, though something to note is that how obvious Path vampires are depends on their Virtues. Honorable Accord vampires are more subtle in their inhumanity because they keep Conscious and Self-Control even if they're still &quot;off&quot; in ways that bug normal people more in behavior and mannerisms than overtly monstrous looks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T19:15:21-08:00","id":1545365,"title":"","content":"And I would say that followers on the Path of Self Focus, Harmony would look very normal as the edicts of the paths strive for blending in. The Road of Heaven depending on what they follow could have appearances that could go both ways. But I never bothered with Paths or Roads with my characters and tried to keep there humanity around 4-6 ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T19:44:16-08:00","id":1545371,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Most everyone I've made up have Humanity, but there are a few who have other moralities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T01:59:34-08:00","id":1545378,"title":"","content":"Page 309, corebook<br /> <br /> &quot;One of the most important themes of Vampire is the Kindred\u2019s struggle to retain their souls and avoid the clutches of the Beast. Thus, it is extremely important to use morality in a consistent, dramatic manner. If the Storyteller allows the players to (sometimes literally) get away with murder, the story will suffer as one of the tragedies of vampiric existence vanishes. If the Story- teller is too strict with the morality rules, though, all the characters will be ravening, blood-gorged maniacs by the end of the first session. Keeping a handle on morality is a hard thing to do, but the degeneration system is designed to help that. (<b>Since most vampires are on Humanity, from this point forward we\u2019ll talk exclusively in those terms</b> \u2014 special rules for those on Paths of Enlightenment start on p. 313.)&quot;<br /> <br /> Aka, when they talk about daysleep and appearance depending on rating of Humanity, it applies to Paths too. They use Humanity when talking about <b>shared features </b>of all Paths of Enlightenment, like daysleep, appearance, etc. <br /> <br /> Differences in perceptiion are due to the bearing, aka, the aura, the supernatural perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28432-misskaos22","name":"MissKaos22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28432_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T04:29:53-08:00","id":1545381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissKaos22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545346-appearance-and-paths?p=1545378#post1545378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 309, corebook<br /> <br /> &quot;One of the most important themes of Vampire is the Kindred\u2019s struggle to retain their souls and avoid the clutches of the Beast. Thus, it is extremely important to use morality in a consistent, dramatic manner. If the Storyteller allows the players to (sometimes literally) get away with murder, the story will suffer as one of the tragedies of vampiric existence vanishes. If the Story- teller is too strict with the morality rules, though, all the characters will be ravening, blood-gorged maniacs by the end of the first session. Keeping a handle on morality is a hard thing to do, but the degeneration system is designed to help that. (<b>Since most vampires are on Humanity, from this point forward we\u2019ll talk exclusively in those terms</b> \u2014 special rules for those on Paths of Enlightenment start on p. 313.)&quot;<br /> <br /> Aka, when they talk about daysleep and appearance depending on rating of Humanity, it applies to Paths too. They use Humanity when talking about <b>shared features </b>of all Paths of Enlightenment, like daysleep, appearance, etc.<br /> <br /> Differences in perceptiion are due to the bearing, aka, the aura, the supernatural perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. And I think it's much better narratively to allow vampires to blend in regardless of Path, and to consider the blending in as a consequence of control over the Beast, regardless of one's moral system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T13:44:09-08:00","id":1545405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissKaos22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545346-appearance-and-paths?p=1545378#post1545378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aka, when they talk about daysleep and appearance depending on rating of Humanity, it applies to Paths too. They use Humanity when talking about <b>shared features </b>of all Paths of Enlightenment, like daysleep, appearance, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be correct when talking about V20, but this is a change from how the game previously dealt with it. The one advantage being on the Path of Humanity had was that you could appear alive. The advantage of the other Paths is that you were more likely to do things fun in an RPG (like killing whoever opposes you) and not have to worry about violating the Path. Allowing all Paths to allow you to look human is a bad design choice in my opinion.<br /> <br /> In earlier editions, the Paths of Enlightenment had limits. Revised corebook said if you are on a Path that you defaulted to a Humanity of 3 (or lower if your Path score was lower) in terms of interacting socially with humans, which included how alive you are. I think that was the better design choice. It's what I would use even if I was running the V20 rules.<br /> <br /> Also, even the V20 corebook in the section on Blood Pool (pg 269) says that &quot;Only vampires with Humanity may use blood in this manner; vampires on a Path have forsaken their human sides entirely.&quot; &quot;This manner&quot; being spending blood points equal to (8 minus Humanity)\u200b to appear alive. So this line specifically contradicts the general rule on page 309. If you can't spend blood to appear alive because you are not on the Path of Humanity, why would you appear alive at all if not on the Path? That would seem to be the logical corollary to me.<br /> <br /> Of course, without a similar statement that Paths default to an appearance of Humanity 3 (which I do not find in V20), you don't have a baseline. But there is something inherently contradictory to me that vampires on a monstrous Path appears fully human if they are truly and utterly dedicated to being monsters while vampires less dedicated to being a monster appear less human.<br /> <br /> Now I will say that not all Paths are equally monstrous. If a Path uses Conscience instead of Conviction (like Honorable Accord or Harmony), I'd be tempted to allow them to appear alive as per the Path rating as if they were on Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T13:58:27-08:00","id":1545406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545346-appearance-and-paths?p=1545405#post1545405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may be correct when talking about V20, but this is a change from how the game previously dealt with it. The one advantage being on the Path of Humanity had was that you could appear alive. The advantage of the other Paths is that you were more likely to do things fun in an RPG (like killing whoever opposes you) and not have to worry about violating the Path. Allowing all Paths to allow you to look human is a bad design choice in my opinion.<br /> <br /> In earlier editions, the Paths of Enlightenment had limits. Revised corebook said if you are on a Path that you defaulted to a Humanity of 3 (or lower if your Path score was lower) in terms of interacting socially with humans, which included how alive you are. I think that was the better design choice. It's what I would use even if I was running the V20 rules.<br /> <br /> Also, even the V20 corebook in the section on Blood Pool (pg 269) says that &quot;Only vampires with Humanity may use blood in this manner; vampires on a Path have forsaken their human sides entirely.&quot; &quot;This manner&quot; being spending blood points equal to (8 minus Humanity) to appear alive. So this line specifically contradicts the general rule on page 309. If you can't spend blood to appear alive because you are not on the Path of Humanity, why would you appear alive at all if not on the Path? That would seem to be the logical corollary to me.<br /> <br /> Of course, without a similar statement that Paths default to an appearance of Humanity 3 (which I do not find in V20), you don't have a baseline. But there is something inherently contradictory to me that vampires on a monstrous Path appears fully human if they are truly and utterly dedicated to being monsters while vampires less dedicated to being a monster appear less human.<br /> <br /> Now I will say that not all Paths are equally monstrous. If a Path uses Conscience instead of Conviction (like Honorable Accord or Harmony), I'd be tempted to allow them to appear alive as per the Path rating as if they were on Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the distinction is rooted in the zombie-like nature of the beast, versus making a conscious choice to be a Dexter Morgan or Hannibal Lectur. The creepiness of the first is obvious, the creepiness of the latter two is relatively subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T19:55:40-08:00","id":1545426,"title":"","content":"And according to retired FBI profiler John Douglas. Dexter and Lector fall under the more dangerous type of serial killer that is the chameleon and can get away for years with their crimes before they slip up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T11:01:54-08:00","id":1545480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545346-appearance-and-paths?p=1545406#post1545406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the distinction is rooted in the zombie-like nature of the beast</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was simply a case when the Beast is strong the vampire is corpselike, but when the Beast is weak the vampire appears alive, why would it be the case that vampires on a Path of Enlightenment cannot spend blood to look alive? In both cases of high score Humanity and other Paths, the Beast is strongly constrained. Yet one can do it and the other cannot.<br /> <br /> I don't think V20 adequately explains this contradiction and tension. I think earlier editions portrayed a more consistent approach.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T12:29:50-08:00","id":1545486,"title":"","content":"While not a Path but a Road, I think the <b>Via Voluptarius</b> the &quot;Path of Pleasure&quot; present a fascinating contradiction<br /> <b>Aconia Messalina</b> a Lasombra woman of intense passions and a sharp mind, formulated the Path of Pleasure in various pieces of lyrical poetry. Moved from Rome to Ancona and actuall became a Prince where she settled in a temple dedicated to Venus, establishing a dynasty of pleasure-priestesses.<br /> High living in the form of vintage vitae, fine clothing, beautiful concubines, and sexual indulgence, feasts and pleasure are the bread and butter of the Road and the Voluptuaries use these sensual things to control their Beast by giving it what it wants, and using the finest things in life to do so as a way to secure this sacrament.<br /> To indulge the vulgar, crass, and ordinary is to go against the ethics<br /> I don't think someone on the Via Voluptarius who uses Conviction and Instinct would be, well, a &quot;sucessfull&quot; sinner without the ability to look alive and enjoy the forbidden pleasures what life could offer...<br /> Same could be said about the &quot;modern&quot; Settite Path, <b>The </b><b>Path of Ecstasy</b> a side branch of the Path of Typhon that requires you to corrupt innocents and wallow in absolute decadence... things that are particualarly impossible if you can't pass as a Human - interrestingly it uses Conscience and Self-Control<br /> <b>Path of Harmony</b>\u200b outright considers a sin to acting too human or too bestial.<br /> The Ashirra's <b>Sharia El-Sama </b>topples this by aside the Path's tennents you also have to keep the Five Pillars of Islam\u200b - and boy as a vampire that is a real challenge! Especially if you can't pass as a Human<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> I think it greatly depends on the Path/Road like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said if the vampire not on Humanity could or could not use blood to look &quot;alive&quot;\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T18:20:24-08:00","id":1545504,"title":"","content":"So, something to consider from page 314 of V20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As opposed to Conscience, which deals with remorse and atonement for Path transgressions, a character with Conviction recognizes his failure and plans to overcome it. Conviction is completely inhuman; the character who has this Trait can no longer pass for human under anything but the most cursory of scrutiny. Creatures who can sense the Beast (vampires, werewolves, etc.) immediately recognize someone with the Conviction Virtue for what he truly is: a monster. Like Conscience, Conviction comes into question when a character must check for degeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T00:37:54-08:00","id":1545519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545346-appearance-and-paths?p=1545504#post1545504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, something to consider from page 314 of V20:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a rule that I have never seen implemented... sadly. And it would have dramatic consequences, as it would become much easier to recognise other vampires without using Auspex or paying attention to breathing or the like.<br /> But this rule, as pointed out in a comment above, is in conflict with the nature, lore and plausibility of several paths.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, I think an ST should decide how they want to handle this in terms of setting: vampires who need to mingle with humans but are evidently inhuman and corpse-like produce a certain type of game. Vampires who can pass for human with little effort unless they're really undisciplined produce another type of game. In fact, not just a type of game, but a type of universe.<br /> And each Path having its distinct Bearing creates another element that must be described and brought into the narrative. It may even be argued that some experienced people may learn to figure out a vampire's Path just by paying attention to how they feel around him, with a difficulty dependent on the vampire's Path rating.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T06:01:15-08:00","id":1545522,"title":"","content":"While I don't inherently disagree, I was just pointing to something in the book in regards to my comment on V20 being a bit mixed in this stuff.<br /> <br /> Though that said, most Paths and Roads meant to involve lots of time with humans are on Conscience, not Conviction. The ViaVoluptarius uses Conviction, but it's members are explicitly reclusive and tend to rely on having trade networks and proxies to get their preferred forms of indulgence(s) brought to them than actively cultivating decadence among the kine. The other examples Shadeprowler brought up are all Conscience Paths, so they wouldn't fall under this rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}